{
  "_README": [
    "Dataset for scripts/compare.py \u2014 100 facts across nine contradiction shapes.",
    "Shapes are drawn from what production agent-memory systems actually resolve:",
    "Zep/Graphiti's bi-temporal invalidation (event time vs ingestion time, validity",
    "windows closed rather than deleted) and Mem0's ADD/UPDATE/DELETE/NOOP operations.",
    "",
    "revisions[0] is the seed, applied sequentially and unmeasured. The rest arrive",
    "concurrently. `answer` is the value a correct memory should return afterwards and",
    "is stated explicitly \u2014 for the out_of_order and tie shapes it is deliberately NOT",
    "the last-ingested revision, which is the whole point of those cases.",
    "",
    "valid_at is the EVENT-time rank of each revision (when the claim was true), as distinct from its position in the list, which is ingestion order. They agree everywhere except the out_of_order shape, where the first-ingested revision has the LATEST event time. Only the Zep/Graphiti-style arm reads this field."
  ],
